From: kang-ingu <kang.ingu@huawei.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HFusionToHIVM: skip result-less MmadL1Op in tile propagation

Backport the two-line guard from upstream commit
f9f4507c4187fe05035a52f1094a6ae602f6bb71 onto CANN 9.1.0 / v1.2.0
(8796a8ac1508380d78128427c61ab47d03f05739).

Buffer-form MmadL1Op has no SSA result. Do not read getResult(0) while
propagating TileMixCubeNum annotations. Add a focused regression test that
keeps the buffer-form operation intact through the conversion pass.

The guard is unchanged from upstream; the regression test is added here.
---
diff --git a/bishengir/lib/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/HFusionToHIVM.cpp b/bishengir/lib/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/HFusionToHIVM.cpp
index ecdaa18f9..557c82b53 100644
--- a/bishengir/lib/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/HFusionToHIVM.cpp
+++ b/bishengir/lib/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/HFusionToHIVM.cpp
@@ -1347,6 +1347,8 @@ public:
     });
 
     moduleOp->walk([&](hivm::MmadL1Op op) {
+      if (op.getNumResults() == 0)
+        return;
       std::optional<Operation *> tileCubeMarkOp =
           utils::getAnnotateOpWithAttr(op.getResult(0), hivm::TileMixCubeNumAttr::name);
       if (tileCubeMarkOp.has_value()) {
diff --git a/bishengir/test/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/mmad-l1-buffer.mlir b/bishengir/test/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/mmad-l1-buffer.mlir
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..a9a09620b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bishengir/test/Conversion/HFusionToHIVM/mmad-l1-buffer.mlir
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+// RUN: bishengir-opt %s -convert-hfusion-to-hivm="mm-map-mode=macro_instr" | FileCheck %s
+
+// Buffer-form MmadL1Op has no SSA result. The TileMixCubeNum propagation
+// walk must leave it intact instead of accessing getResult(0).
+// CHECK-LABEL: func.func @mmad_l1_buffer
+// CHECK: hivm.hir.mmadL1
+// CHECK-SAME: outs({{.*}} : memref<16x16xf32>)
+// CHECK: return
+func.func @mmad_l1_buffer(%a: memref<16x16xf16>,
+                          %b: memref<16x16xf16>,
+                          %c: memref<16x16xf32>) {
+  %false = arith.constant false
+  %c0 = arith.constant 0 : index
+  hivm.hir.mmadL1 ins(%a, %b, %false, %c0, %c0, %c0 :
+      memref<16x16xf16>, memref<16x16xf16>, i1, index, index, index)
+    outs(%c : memref<16x16xf32>)
+  return
+}
